Ingrid drinks 8 cups of water daily. Over 30 days, she consumes:

\[
8 \, \text{cups/day} \times 30 \, \text{days} = 240 \, \text{cups}
\]

Converting cups to gallons (16 cups/gallon):

\[
\frac{240 \, \text{cups}}{16 \, \text{cups/gallon}} = 15 \, \text{gallons}
\]

\boxed{15}
